      "sender": "SYSTEM",
      "recipient": "USER",
      "content": "{{USER_INSTRUCTION}}ROUND 1 [provide: image_1, image_2, image_3, image_4, image_5, image_6]\nQuery: I'm setting up a nature scavenger hunt and contest. Look at the contest sign in the second image. Create a Todoist project named 'Wildlife Event' and add a task to purchase the exact 1st prize listed there.\nInstructions: Tell the agent to create the 'Wildlife Event' project and add a task to buy the 1st prize shown in the contest sign image. If the agent asks for the specific prize details, direct it to read the 1st prize text from the sign in the second image. Once the project and task are created, move to the next round.\n\nROUND 2\nQuery: Identify the fungus in the first image and the plant in the fourth image. Add two tasks to the project: 'Photograph [fungus name]' and 'Photograph [plant name]'.\nInstructions: Ask the agent to identify the specific species of the fungus and the pink flower from the first and fourth images, respectively. Instruct it to add two separate tasks to the 'Wildlife Event' project to photograph each of those species. If the agent cannot identify them immediately, encourage it to use its web search tools to find the names based on their appearance. Once both tasks are added, proceed to the next round.\n\nROUND 3\nQuery: Now identify the dog, the fish, and the gecko from the remaining images. Create a parent task called 'Fauna Checkpoints' and add the three identified species as sub-tasks under it.\nInstructions: Instruct the agent to identify the dog breed, the fish species, and the gecko species from the remaining three images. Tell it to create a new task called 'Fauna Checkpoints' in the project, and then add the three identified animals as sub-tasks. If the agent needs help, tell it to search online based on the visual features. Proceed when the parent task and all three sub-tasks are created.\n\nROUND 4\nQuery: I realized the dog isn't a wild animal. Delete its sub-task. Then, send a text message to Alex summarizing our final list of scavenger hunt targets and the 1st prize we are giving out.\nInstructions: Tell the agent to delete the sub-task for the dog, since it doesn't fit the wild animal theme. Then, ask it to send a text message to Alex with a summary of the final four targets (the two plants and the two remaining animals) and the specific 1st prize being awarded. The assistant should find multiple contacts named Alex and ask for clarification or present a selection. When it does, select Alex Johnson (the event coordinator) via `ui_user_interact`. If no interactive UI is shown, tell the assistant you mean Alex Johnson. Conclude the conversation once the message is sent.\n\nYou have 6 images available to share with the agent using the send_message_with_image tool.\nIMPORTANT: Image IDs are ZERO-INDEXED integers (0, 1, 2, ...). Do NOT add 1 to the IDs.\nAvailable image IDs: [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]\nImage mapping:\n  image_1.jpg -> image ID 0\n  image_2.jpg -> image ID 1\n  image_3.jpg -> image ID 2\n  image_4.jpg -> image ID 3\n  image_5.jpg -> image ID 4\n  image_6.jpg -> image ID 5"
    },
